{
  "framework": "nextjs",
  "frameworkDetail": "Next.js 14.2.5 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript ^5.5, Tailwind 3.4.6. Confirmed from package.json dependencies/devDependencies. No state/persistence libraries present (no dexie/idb/localforage/zustand-persist/sqlite equivalents).",
  "dataLayerPattern": "Every domain API module lives at src/lib/api/<domain>.ts and exports a small set of async functions (either a flat object like `xApi` or named exports) that components import — never `fetch()` directly in a component. Two sub-patterns exist, both routed through src/lib/api/client.ts: (1) PURE MOCK DELEGATION — the majority of domain files (communities, creator-content, dm, earnings, explore, kyc, learn, marketplace, mentors, messaging, profile, services, settings, subscription, tips, verification) call straight into a sibling src/lib/api/mocks/<domain>.ts module with no network attempt, using `mockRequest(data, delayMs)` from client.ts to simulate round-trip latency. (2) TRY-FETCH-THEN-MOCK-FALLBACK — a smaller set (auth, content, notifications, purchases, search) first call `apiFetch(path)` (also in client.ts) inside a try block and fall back to the mock module in the catch. This works today because `USE_MOCKS` (src/lib/api/config.ts) is true whenever NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is unset (the current default) or NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=true is forced — in that mode apiFetch throws a MockModeError immediately so the fallback fires with no network round trip. When a real backend is wired up (API_BASE set), the try branch will actually hit the network and only fall back to mocks on failure. Almost every mock read is annotated with a `// SEAM: replace with <METHOD> /api/hub/...` comment marking the exact intended real endpoint and verb — this comment is the frontend's own contract documentation. Mock data itself is plain in-memory module-level JS (arrays/objects), sometimes mutated directly (e.g. currentSession, kycSubmission) to simulate writes; no backing store, resets on every page reload.",
  "dataLayerPaths": ["src/lib/api/", "src/lib/api/mocks/"],
  "exampleFiles": [
    "src/lib/api/dm.ts imports getMockDmThread/getMockDmThreads/getMockUnreadDmCount/sendMockPaidDm from ./mocks/dm.ts — pure delegation pattern, every export SEAM-tagged.",
    "src/lib/api/content.ts imports mockContent/mockContentById/mockPurchasedIds from ./mocks/mockContent.ts, wrapped in try{apiFetch(...)}catch{...mock fallback, SEAM-tagged} — try-fetch-then-mock pattern.",
    "src/lib/api/communities.ts and src/lib/api/mocks/communities.ts show the pattern duplicated at both layers: the outer file re-exports thin wrappers around the mock functions, and the mock file itself carries a second, identical set of SEAM comments (the source of truth) — this double-tagging (outer wrapper + inner mock) recurs across communities, dm, explore, learn, mentors, verification, settings.",
    "src/lib/api/subscription.ts + src/components/subscription/SubscriptionManagement.tsx: subscription.ts is pure mock delegation via mockRequest(); the component itself also carries one inline SEAM-tagged mock array (BILLING_HISTORY) that hasn't been promoted into mocks/ yet, showing the 'inline literal not yet in mocks/' variant of the same pattern."
  ],
  "localPersistence": {
    "present": false,
    "reason": "No persistence package in package.json (deps are only next/react/react-dom/lucide-react; devDeps are typecheck/lint/build tooling only — no dexie, idb, localforage, or sqlite-equivalent). grep of src/ for localStorage|IndexedDB|indexedDB|dexie|sqlite|idb found exactly one hit, a doc-comment in src/lib/auth/session-storage.ts stating persistence will be ADDED later ('When the real backend exists, restore persistence (e.g. localStorage or a refresh token) here') — i.e. it is explicitly NOT implemented today. All app state (session, mock data mutations) is plain in-memory JS module state that resets on full page reload. Session/token storage (src/lib/auth/session-storage.ts, wrapped by src/lib/auth/session-provider.tsx) is also in-memory only, not sessionStorage/localStorage despite the variable name `sessionStorage` — it's a hand-rolled module-scope store, not the browser Web Storage API. This is auth-token bookkeeping, not application data provenance, and is called out separately from dataProvenance per instructions."
  },
