  "mockDataPatternDescription": "For any given screen: (1) find its route file(s) under src/app/, (2) find which src/lib/api/<domain>.ts function(s) it or its child components import, (3) open that domain file — it is either a thin pass-through to src/lib/api/mocks/<domain>.ts (majority) or a try{apiFetch}catch{mock} wrapper (auth, content, notifications, purchases, search), (4) the actual seed literals live in the mocks/ file, always plain exported consts/arrays/objects, occasionally mutated in place (currentSession in mocks/session.ts, kycSubmission in mocks/kyc.ts) to fake writes. Every mock read is SEAM-tagged with the real endpoint it will become — treat that comment as authoritative for the contract shape. A handful of screens/components have NOT yet promoted their literals into mocks/: these appear as inline const arrays/objects directly in the .tsx file, sometimes still SEAM-tagged (e.g. SubscriptionManagement.tsx's BILLING_HISTORY) and sometimes not (e.g. Explore's SHOPS stat counts, HomeRightRail/CreatorDashboard/EarningsDashboard's hardcoded '1,240' EVG value). Treat SEAM-tagged inline literals the same as a mocks/ file for extraction purposes; treat un-tagged inline literals as needing a judgment call — flagged individually below.",
